# Introduction

The **Standalone Signer** lets any application add qualified (QES) or advanced (AdES) signatures and electronic seals to PDF documents with one backend call, one embeddable signing component and one webhook. You do not integrate trust service providers, identification, PAdES, certificates or timestamping: the Standalone Signer and the ViziBit Signing Service handle all of that.

This guide is the starting point for every integration of the Standalone Signer. It is written for partners integrating the service into their products and for ViziBit teams building or supporting integrations.

**Your integration does three things:**

1. **Backend — create a signature request.** Send the PDF, the signing policy (level and allowed providers) and two webhook URLs. You receive a `signatureRequestId` and a per-document `signatureToken`.
2. **Frontend — let the user sign.** Embed the JavaScript SDK with the `signatureToken`. The signer previews the document, places the signature and signs with one of the providers you allowed. The signer never logs in to a ViziBit product.
3. **Backend — complete.** Receive the webhook, download the signed PDF and store it.

**What the Standalone Signer does not do:** it does not orchestrate multi-party workflows (signing order, signer replacement, reminders, escalations). One signature request produces one signature. Your application chains requests when a document needs several signatures (see [Several signatures on one document](#several-signatures-on-one-document)).

<aside class="notice">
The base URL of your environment and your API credentials (<code>client_id</code> / <code>client_secret</code>) are provided by ViziBit for each integration team. In this guide they appear as the placeholders <code>{{SIGNER_HOST}}</code>, <code>{{CLIENT_ID}}</code> and <code>{{CLIENT_SECRET}}</code>.
</aside>

## Base URL and environments

All API endpoints share the prefix `/v/1/signature/standalone` on the Standalone Signer host; the SDK and the web pages are served under `/signature/standalone`.

| Environment | Base URL | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Sandbox | `https://{{SIGNER_HOST}}/v/1/signature/standalone` | Provided with your sandbox credentials. Use it for development and testing. |
| Production (cloud) | `https://{{SIGNER_HOST}}/v/1/signature/standalone` | Provided when you go live. |
| On-premise | defined by your installation | Same API. See [On-premise installations](#on-premise-installations). |

Other useful URLs on every host:

| URL | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `https://{{SIGNER_HOST}}/v/1/signature/standalone/swagger` | Swagger UI / OpenAPI description |
| `https://{{SIGNER_HOST}}/v/1/signature/standalone/health/basic` | Liveness |
| `https://{{SIGNER_HOST}}/v/1/signature/standalone/health/ready` | Readiness |
| `https://{{SIGNER_HOST}}/signature/standalone/sdk/signator-signer-sdk.js` | JavaScript SDK |
| `https://{{SIGNER_HOST}}/signature/standalone/sdk-test.html` | SDK test harness |
| `https://{{SIGNER_HOST}}/signature/standalone/` | Signature request dashboard (sign in with your API client) |
| `https://{{SIGNER_HOST}}/signature/standalone/admin.html` | API client administration |

## Concepts

| Concept | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **API client** | Your application's identity: `client_id` and `client_secret`. Used only by your **backend**. Each client sees only its own signature requests. A client can belong to a **partner** (used to aggregate usage) and can have its organisation's **seals** assigned to it; the ViziBit electronic seal is available to every client. |
| **Access token** | OAuth2 bearer token obtained with the client credentials (valid 1 hour). Authorises the backend endpoints. |
| **Signature request** | One PDF waiting for one signature, identified by `signatureRequestId`. It carries the **signing policy** you defined: level, allowed providers, jurisdiction, seal, signer phone number and whether identification is allowed. |
| **Signature token** | JWT returned when a request is created. It is scoped to that one request and valid until the request expires. It authorises the signing UI (preview, sign, reject, status) for that document only, so it is safe to hand to the signer's browser. |
| **Webhooks** | Two URLs you supply per request. The service calls one of them when the request reaches its outcome. |
| **External reference** | Your own identifier for the document (e.g. a contract id). It is returned in every response and webhook and is searchable in the dashboard. |

## Signature levels and providers

The level and the providers the signer may use are decided by **your backend** when it creates the request. The signing UI can only choose among the providers you allowed; it can never change the level, the seal, the jurisdiction or the phone number.

| `signatureLevel` | Meaning | Allowed `providers` |
|---|---|---|
| `QES` | Qualified electronic signature (legal equivalent of a handwritten signature in the EU) | `FinaRiws`, `CertiliaSdurddV1`, `CertiliaCommercialV1`, `LocalComponentV1`, `SwisscomEtsiV1`, `ATrustCscV1` |
| `AES` | Advanced electronic signature | `SwisscomEtsiV1`, `LocalComponentV1` |
| `SES` | Electronic seal applied without user interaction: the ViziBit electronic seal or your organisation's seal (see [Electronic seals](#electronic-seals)) | none — the seal is selected with `sealId` |

| Provider | What the signer uses | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `FinaRiws` | FINA remote signature, approved on the signer's mobile device | `signer.phoneNumber` is **required**. QES only. |
| `CertiliaSdurddV1` | Certilia (AKD) remote signing with the national identity card (eOI) certificate | QES only. |
| `CertiliaCommercialV1` | Certilia (AKD) commercial cloud certificate | QES only. |
| `LocalComponentV1` | Smart card or USB token (e.g. FINA or AKD cards) through the ViziBit local component installed on the signer's computer | QES, or AES when the request asks for AES. |
| `SwisscomEtsiV1` | Swisscom remote signature, including Swisscom's own online or video identification | QES or AES. `jurisdiction` `EIDAS` (default) or `ZERTES` (Swiss law). Optional `signer.phoneNumber` as login hint. |
| `ATrustCscV1` | A-Trust (ID Austria) | QES only. |

Signatures are embedded in the PDF as PAdES signatures with a trusted timestamp. Only the document hash leaves the Standalone Signer; the PDF itself is never sent to the provider.

<aside class="notice">
For providers that read the certificate from the signer's own device (<code>LocalComponentV1</code>), the legal level of the resulting signature depends on the certificate the signer uses. Requesting <code>AES</code> records the signature as advanced.
</aside>

# Integration flow

```text
 Your backend            Your frontend + SDK          Standalone Signer          Provider
 ------------            -------------------          -----------------          --------
 1  POST /connect/token  ─────────────────────────────▶ access_token
 2  POST /integration    ─────────────────────────────▶ { signatureRequestId,
    (PDF, policy, webhooks)                               signatureToken }
 3  hand signatureToken ─▶ SignatorSigner.create(...)
 4                         GET /pdf/state, /pdf/download ▶ policy + PDF preview
 5                         signer clicks "Sign" (chooses provider if several)
 6                         POST /pdf/init ───────────────▶ QES/AES: hash ───────────▶ consent page
 7                         (SDK sends signer to the provider, signer approves)     ◀─ signed hash
 8                                                        embed signature + timestamp
 9  ◀──────────────────────────────────────── webhook { state: "Signed", ... }
10  GET /integration/{id}/document ────────────────────▶ signed PDF
11  DELETE /integration/{id}/document (optional)
```

1. Your backend obtains an access token with its client credentials.
2. Your backend creates a signature request with the PDF, the signing policy and the webhook URLs, and stores the returned `signatureRequestId` and `signatureToken` with its own document.
3. Your frontend asks your backend for the `signatureToken` of the document the user should sign and mounts the SDK with it.
4. The SDK loads the signing policy and the PDF.
5. The signer places the signature (optional) and clicks **Sign**. When several providers are allowed, the SDK asks which one to use.
6. For QES/AES the Standalone Signer sends the document hash to the provider; for SES it seals immediately.
7. The SDK sends the signer to the provider's consent page; the signer authenticates and approves.
8. The Standalone Signer embeds the signature and timestamp into the PDF.
9. Your backend receives the webhook with the outcome.
10. Your backend downloads the signed PDF.
11. Optionally, your backend deletes the copy kept by the Standalone Signer.

## Request states

| State | Meaning | Terminal |
|---|---|---|
| `Initialized` | Created, waiting for the signer. | no |
| `WaitingForUserApproval` | Signing started; the signer is at the provider. | no |
| `Signed` | The document is signed; the success webhook is being delivered. | yes (success) |
| `Finished` | Signed and the success webhook was processed. Treat it exactly like `Signed`. | yes (success) |
| `Failed` | The provider or the signing failed. | yes |
| `Rejected` | The signer or your backend rejected the request. | yes |
| `Expired` | `expiresAt` passed before the request was signed. | yes |

```text
                    POST /pdf/init (SES)
 Initialized ──────────────────────────────────────────────▶ Signed ──▶ Finished
     │  POST /pdf/init (QES/AES)                                ▲
     ▼                                                          │ provider signed
 WaitingForUserApproval ────────────────────────────────────────┘
     │  provider error / timeout ─▶ Failed
     │  reject (signer or backend) ─▶ Rejected
     └─ expiresAt passed ─▶ Expired   (also from Initialized)
```

* A QES/AES ceremony waits up to 90 minutes for the signer at the provider and then fails.
* A request reaches exactly one outcome. Late or duplicate provider results after that are ignored.
* A failed, rejected or expired request cannot be signed again: create a new request.
* Deleting the stored document does not change the state; it sets `documentDeletedAt`.

# Authentication

There are **two different bearer tokens**:

| Token | How you get it | Used for | Who may hold it |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Access token** | `POST /connect/token` with your `client_id` and `client_secret` | All `/integration/*` endpoints, `/usage`, `/dashboard/*`, `/admin/*` | Your backend only |
| **Signature token** | Returned by `POST /integration` | The `/pdf/*` endpoints used by the SDK | Your backend and the signer's browser |

Sending an access token to a `/pdf/*` endpoint returns `401` with `errorCode` `30019`.

## Get an access token

```shell
curl -X POST "https://{{SIGNER_HOST}}/v/1/signature/standalone/connect/token" \
  -d grant_type=client_credentials \
  -d client_id={{CLIENT_ID}} \
  -d client_secret={{CLIENT_SECRET}}
```

```csharp
using var http = new HttpClient { BaseAddress = new Uri("https://{{SIGNER_HOST}}/v/1/signature/standalone/") };

var tokenResponse = await http.PostAsync("connect/token", new FormUrlEncodedContent(new Dictionary<string, string>
{
    ["grant_type"] = "client_credentials",
    ["client_id"] = "{{CLIENT_ID}}",
    ["client_secret"] = "{{CLIENT_SECRET}}"
}));
tokenResponse.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
var token = await tokenResponse.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<JsonElement>();
var accessToken = token.GetProperty("access_token").GetString();
```

```javascript
// Node.js 18+ (backend only — never expose the client secret to a browser)
const res = await fetch('https://{{SIGNER_HOST}}/v/1/signature/standalone/connect/token', {
  method: 'POST',
  body: new URLSearchParams({
    grant_type: 'client_credentials',
    client_id: '{{CLIENT_ID}}',
    client_secret: '{{CLIENT_SECRET}}'
  })
});
const { access_token: accessToken } = await res.json();
```

> Response

```json
{
  "access_token": "eyJhbGciOi…",
  "token_type": "Bearer",
  "expires_in": 3600
}
```

`POST /v/1/signature/standalone/connect/token`

Standard OAuth2 client credentials grant (`application/x-www-form-urlencoded`). HTTP Basic client authentication (`Authorization: Basic base64(client_id:client_secret)`) is also accepted.

Cache the access token until shortly before `expires_in` elapses instead of requesting one per call.

## Credentials

* ViziBit creates your API client and gives you the `client_id` and `client_secret` per integration team and environment. The secret is shown once; store it in a secret manager.
* You can rotate your own secret at any time: `POST /admin/clients/{{CLIENT_ID}}/rotate-secret` with body `{}` returns a new random secret (see [Administration](#administration-api-clients)).
* Never put the client secret in a browser or mobile app. The browser only ever receives a signature token.

# Signature requests

Backend endpoints. All require the **access token** (`Authorization: Bearer <access_token>`). JSON bodies are read case-insensitively; responses use camelCase. Binary content (`document`, image data) is base64.

## Create a signature request

```shell
curl -X POST "https://{{SIGNER_HOST}}/v/1/signature/standalone/integration" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS_TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "document": "JVBERi0xLjcK…",
    "documentName": "Employment contract - Ivana Horvat.pdf",
    "externalReference": "hr/contracts/4711",
    "signatureLevel": "QES",
    "providers": ["FinaRiws", "CertiliaSdurddV1", "LocalComponentV1"],
    "signer": { "phoneNumber": "+385911234567" },
    "signatureImage": {
      "page": 3, "widgetOffsetX": 355, "widgetOffsetY": 40,
      "widgetWidth": 200, "widgetHeight": 70,
      "appearance": 1, "lineOne": "Ivana Horvat", "lineTwo": "Employee"
    },
    "callbacks": {
      "onSigned": "https://app.example.com/hooks/signature/signed",
      "onError": "https://app.example.com/hooks/signature/error",
      "authorizationHeader": "Bearer 6f1c0b4e9a2d…"
    },
    "expiresAt": "2026-12-31T23:00:00Z"
  }'
```

```csharp
var request = new
{
    document = Convert.ToBase64String(pdfBytes),
    documentName = "Employment contract - Ivana Horvat.pdf",
    externalReference = "hr/contracts/4711",
    signatureLevel = "QES",
    providers = new[] { "FinaRiws", "CertiliaSdurddV1", "LocalComponentV1" },
    signer = new { phoneNumber = "+385911234567" },
    callbacks = new
    {
        onSigned = "https://app.example.com/hooks/signature/signed",
        onError = "https://app.example.com/hooks/signature/error",
        authorizationHeader = $"Bearer {webhookSecret}"
    },
    expiresAt = DateTimeOffset.UtcNow.AddDays(7)
};

http.DefaultRequestHeaders.Authorization = new AuthenticationHeaderValue("Bearer", accessToken);
var response = await http.PostAsJsonAsync("integration", request);
response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode(); // 201 Created
var created = await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<JsonElement>();
var signatureRequestId = created.GetProperty("signatureRequestId").GetGuid();
var signatureToken = created.GetProperty("signatureToken").GetString();
```

```javascript
const res = await fetch('https://{{SIGNER_HOST}}/v/1/signature/standalone/integration', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${accessToken}`, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    document: pdfBuffer.toString('base64'),
    documentName: 'Employment contract - Ivana Horvat.pdf',
    externalReference: 'hr/contracts/4711',
    signatureLevel: 'QES',
    providers: ['FinaRiws', 'CertiliaSdurddV1', 'LocalComponentV1'],
    signer: { phoneNumber: '+385911234567' },
    callbacks: {
      onSigned: 'https://app.example.com/hooks/signature/signed',
      onError: 'https://app.example.com/hooks/signature/error',
      authorizationHeader: `Bearer ${webhookSecret}`
    },
    expiresAt: new Date(Date.now() + 7 * 24 * 3600 * 1000).toISOString()
  })
});
if (res.status !== 201) throw new Error(`Create failed: ${res.status} ${await res.text()}`);
const { signatureRequestId, signatureToken } = await res.json();
```

> Response `201 Created` (header `Location: /v/1/signature/standalone/integration/{signatureRequestId}`)

```json
{
  "signatureRequestId": "3f1c7d2a-5a6e-4f5e-9d0b-0d7e9b1c2a11",
  "signatureToken": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIs…",
  "state": "Initialized",
  "expiresAt": "2026-12-31T23:00:00Z",
  "signatureLevel": "QES",
  "providers": ["FinaRiws", "CertiliaSdurddV1", "LocalComponentV1"],
  "jurisdiction": "EIDAS",
  "sealId": null,
  "allowIdentification": false,
  "lockSignaturePosition": false,
  "documentName": "Employment contract - Ivana Horvat.pdf",
  "externalReference": "hr/contracts/4711"
}
```

`POST /v/1/signature/standalone/integration`

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `document` | string (base64) | yes | The PDF to sign. |
| `documentName` | string (≤ 255) | no | File name used for downloads and shown on the dashboard. Folder parts are removed. |
| `externalReference` | string (≤ 256) | no | Your identifier for the document. Returned in responses and webhooks; searchable in the dashboard; never shown to the signer. |
| `signatureLevel` | string | yes | `QES`, `AES` or `SES`. |
| `providers` | string[] | QES/AES | Providers the signer may use, in the order they are offered. See [Signature levels and providers](#signature-levels-and-providers). Not allowed for `SES`. |
| `jurisdiction` | string | no | `EIDAS` (default) or `ZERTES`. `ZERTES` (Swiss law) requires `SwisscomEtsiV1` as the only provider. Not used for `SES`. |
| `sealId` | string | no | Seal to apply (SES only): `Generic` for the ViziBit electronic seal, available to every API client, or a seal assigned to your client. When omitted: your client's seal if exactly one is assigned, otherwise `Generic` if none is assigned; required when several are assigned. See [Electronic seals](#electronic-seals). Not allowed for QES/AES. |
| `signer.phoneNumber` | string | for `FinaRiws` | The signer's mobile number in international format (e.g. `+385911234567`; spaces, dashes and parentheses are removed). Required when `FinaRiws` is allowed; optional login hint for `SwisscomEtsiV1`. Ignored when no allowed provider uses it, and kept only until signing starts. |
| `allowIdentification` | boolean | no | Lets a signer without a digital identity start remote identification from the signing UI. QES/AES only. See [Identification](#identification-of-signers-without-a-digital-identity). |
| `signatureImage` | object | no | Position and appearance of the visible signature. With a position, the signer sees it there as soon as the document opens. See [Signature appearance](#signature-appearance). Without it the signature is invisible unless the signer places one. |
| `lockSignaturePosition` | boolean | no | Fixes the signature at the position in `signatureImage` (page, offsets and size required): the signer cannot move or resize it and the signing UI cannot send another placement. |
| `callbacks.onSigned` | URL | yes | Absolute `http`/`https` URL called when the document is signed. |
| `callbacks.onError` | URL | yes | Absolute `http`/`https` URL called when signing failed, was rejected or expired. |
| `callbacks.method` | string | no | `POST` (default), `PUT`, `PATCH` or `DELETE`. |
| `callbacks.authorizationHeader` | string (≤ 4096) | no | Sent verbatim as the `Authorization` header of both webhooks. Use a random secret per request. |
| `expiresAt` | string / number | no | Deadline as ISO 8601 date-time or Unix time in **seconds** (not milliseconds — JavaScript `Date.now()` must be divided by 1000). Default: 2 days after creation. Must be at least one minute in the future and at most 90 days ahead. |

Store `signatureRequestId`, `signatureToken`, your webhook secret and `expiresAt` together with your document.

<aside class="warning">
<code>expiresAt</code> also ends the life of the signature token and of the stored PDF: after it passes, the request is expired if still unsigned and the stored document (signed or not) is deleted. Download the signed PDF as soon as you receive the success webhook.
</aside>

### Signing policy rules

* `signatureLevel` is required; `QES` and `AES` need at least one provider; `SES` takes no providers.
* `AES` is available only with `SwisscomEtsiV1` and `LocalComponentV1`. Any other provider returns `400` with `errorCode` `53`.
* Unknown providers, or providers not available in the Standalone Signer, return `400` with `errorCode` `186`.
* `FinaRiws` requires `signer.phoneNumber`.
* `ZERTES` is only possible when `SwisscomEtsiV1` is the only provider; `SES` takes no jurisdiction.
* `SES` uses the ViziBit electronic seal (`Generic`) or a seal assigned to your API client. Any other seal returns `403` (`errorCode` `205`); omitting `sealId` while several seals are assigned returns `400` (`errorCode` `275`).
* `allowIdentification` is rejected for `SES`.
* Everything in the policy is fixed when the request is created. The signing UI may only choose one of `providers`.

### Signature appearance

> Visible signature: 200 × 70 pt box, 40 pt from the right and bottom edges of an A4 page

```json
{
  "page": 3,
  "widgetOffsetX": 355,
  "widgetOffsetY": 40,
  "widgetWidth": 200,
  "widgetHeight": 70,
  "appearance": 1,
  "lineOne": "Ivana Horvat",
  "lineTwo": "Employee",
  "useHandwrittenStyle": true
}
```

The `signatureImage` object describes where the visible signature goes and what it looks like. The signature is visible when `widgetOffsetX` and `widgetOffsetY` are set.

| Field | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `page` | int | 1-based page number. |
| `widgetOffsetX` | number | Distance in PDF points (1/72 inch) from the left edge of the page. |
| `widgetOffsetY` | number | Distance in PDF points from the **bottom** edge of the page to the bottom of the box. |
| `widgetWidth`, `widgetHeight` | number | Size of the box in PDF points. Always set both. |
| `appearance` | **number** | `1` = card generated by ViziBit (default, embedded as vector graphics); `0` = your image as-is. Send the number, not a string. |
| `lineOne` … `lineFour` | string | Text lines of the generated card (name, role, company…). |
| `useHandwrittenStyle` | bool | Card: render `lineOne` in a handwriting font. |
| `logoImageData` | base64 | Card: optional logo. |
| `imageData` | base64 | Image (PNG or JPEG) when `appearance` is `0`. |
| `fileType` | number | `0` = JPEG, `1` = PNG (with `appearance` `0`). |

An A4 page is 595 × 842 points. A box in the bottom-right corner with 40 pt margins: `widgetOffsetX = 595 − 40 − width`, `widgetOffsetY = 40`.

**Presetting the signature:** when `signatureImage` has a position, the SDK draws the signature at that position as soon as the document opens; the signer does not have to place it.

* **Suggested position** (default): the signer may drag or resize it before clicking **Sign**; only the new position is sent, the appearance stays yours.
* **Fixed position:** add `"lockSignaturePosition": true`, e.g. for the signature field of a contract template. The signer sees the signature where it will be applied and can only click **Sign**; the Standalone Signer rejects any other placement (`403`).
* **No position:** the signature is invisible unless the signer places one with the SDK.

If you pass your own `signatureText` or `signatureImage` to the SDK instead, the SDK appearance is used (unless the request locks the position), starting at `signaturePosition` or the position from the create call.

`POST /v/1/signature/standalone/signature_image/preview` (no authentication) takes the same object and returns a PNG preview of the generated card.

## Get a signature request

```shell
curl "https://{{SIGNER_HOST}}/v/1/signature/standalone/integration/3f1c7d2a-5a6e-4f5e-9d0b-0d7e9b1c2a11" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS_TOKEN"
```

```csharp
var details = await http.GetFromJsonAsync<JsonElement>($"integration/{signatureRequestId}");
var state = details.GetProperty("state").GetString();
var signed = details.GetProperty("signed").GetBoolean();
```

```javascript
const res = await fetch(`https://{{SIGNER_HOST}}/v/1/signature/standalone/integration/${signatureRequestId}`, {
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${accessToken}` }
});
const details = await res.json();
```

> Response `200 OK`

```json
{
  "signatureRequestId": "3f1c7d2a-5a6e-4f5e-9d0b-0d7e9b1c2a11",
  "clientId": "{{CLIENT_ID}}",
  "partner": "acme-partner",
  "externalReference": "hr/contracts/4711",
  "documentName": "Employment contract - Ivana Horvat.pdf",
  "state": "Finished",
  "signed": true,
  "signatureLevel": "QES",
  "providers": ["FinaRiws", "CertiliaSdurddV1", "LocalComponentV1"],
  "provider": "FinaRiws",
  "jurisdiction": "EIDAS",
  "sealId": null,
  "allowIdentification": false,
  "lockSignaturePosition": false,
  "createdAt": "2026-11-24T10:00:00Z",
  "signedAt": "2026-11-24T10:04:12Z",
  "finishedAt": "2026-11-24T10:04:12Z",
  "expiresAt": "2026-12-31T23:00:00Z",
  "documentDeletedAt": null,
  "errorCode": null,
  "message": null
}
```

`GET /v/1/signature/standalone/integration/{signatureRequestId}`

Returns the full status of one of your requests. Use it to reconcile lost webhooks or to show progress in your UI. `provider` is the provider the signer actually used (`GenericPkcs12Seal` for seals). Requests of other API clients return `404`.

## Download the document

```shell
curl "https://{{SIGNER_HOST}}/v/1/signature/standalone/integration/3f1c7d2a-5a6e-4f5e-9d0b-0d7e9b1c2a11/document" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS_TOKEN" -o signed.pdf
```

```csharp
var pdf = await http.GetByteArrayAsync($"integration/{signatureRequestId}/document");
await File.WriteAllBytesAsync("signed.pdf", pdf);
```

```javascript
const res = await fetch(`https://{{SIGNER_HOST}}/v/1/signature/standalone/integration/${signatureRequestId}/document`, {
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${accessToken}` }
});
const pdf = Buffer.from(await res.arrayBuffer());
```

`GET /v/1/signature/standalone/integration/{signatureRequestId}/document`

Returns the current PDF (`application/pdf`, with a `Content-Disposition` file name): the original before signing, the **signed** PDF once the state is `Signed` or `Finished`. Returns `410` (`errorCode` `30016`) after the document was deleted.

## Reject (cancel) a request

```shell
curl -X POST "https://{{SIGNER_HOST}}/v/1/signature/standalone/integration/3f1c7d2a-5a6e-4f5e-9d0b-0d7e9b1c2a11/reject" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS_TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{ "reason": "Contract withdrawn" }'
```

```csharp
await http.PostAsJsonAsync($"integration/{signatureRequestId}/reject", new { reason = "Contract withdrawn" });
```

```javascript
await fetch(`https://{{SIGNER_HOST}}/v/1/signature/standalone/integration/${signatureRequestId}/reject`, {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${accessToken}`, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ reason: 'Contract withdrawn' })
});
```

`POST /v/1/signature/standalone/integration/{signatureRequestId}/reject`

Withdraws a request that has not been signed yet (e.g. the document was replaced). The state becomes `Rejected`, the error webhook is sent with `errorCode` `StandaloneIntegrationSignatureRejected` and your `reason` as `message`. Returns `204`; `409` if the request already reached an outcome. The body is optional.

## Delete the stored document

`DELETE /v/1/signature/standalone/integration/{signatureRequestId}/document`

Deletes the PDF kept by the Standalone Signer once you have stored the signed copy. Allowed only when the request is no longer in progress (`409` otherwise). Returns `204`. Documents are deleted automatically when `expiresAt` passes.

